# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets.  This repository is PUBLIC.  Nothing matching these may be added.
#
# These patterns are a guard against an accidental `git add -A`, not a
# guarantee: `git add -f` overrides them, and tools that are not git do not
# consult them at all.  Credentials should live outside the working tree
# entirely -- a password manager, or a directory that is not a git repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*[Rr]ecovery-[Cc]odes*
*[Rr]ecovery_[Cc]odes*
*RecoveryCodes*
*[Cc]redential*
*[Ss]ecret*
*_token*
*-token*
.pypirc
.netrc
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Byproducts of running things.  These were path-scoped before, which let a
# stray sv.log at the repository root through; the patterns are global now.
# Note there is deliberately no global *.toc rule: stata/stata.toc is a
# package file, not a LaTeX table of contents.
*.log
*.aux
*.out
*.smcl
docs/*.toc

# docs/vignette.pdf is committed on purpose -- it is a deliverable, and not
# everyone reading the repository has a LaTeX toolchain.

# Scratch do-files from earlier debugging
validation/lic.do
validation/test1.do

.DS_Store

# the upstream clones live here for reference; they are separate projects
Copula-based-endogeneity-corrections/
endogCopula/
